  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'These big machines are servers


    When you host a game, your computer
    becomes the server. That means your PC is the one keeping the match running,
    tracking players, and sending out the game information.


    Anyone who joins
    your session becomes a client. Their computers connect to yours, receive updates
    from your server, and send their actions back. This is the same basic idea real
    network engineers work with every day. A server provides, and clients connect.


    Understanding
    this is a big first step toward learning how real networks work in the real world.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
